<h2 class="bde-heading-506-128 bde-heading">
Why Do the 76ers Pay VJ Edgecombe Rookie Money?
</h2><div class="bde-fancy-container-506-129 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-fancy-container-506-145 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-f-text-506-158 bde-f-text">
<p>Edgecombe is paid <strong>$11.66m</strong> because the rookie scale pays by draft position, and the third pick is near the top of it.</p>
<ul>
<li>He went third in 2025, the same slot <a href="/players/joel-embiid/">Joel Embiid</a> and <a href="/players/jaylen-brown/">Jaylen Brown</a> were taken in.</li>
<li>The four years are worth <strong>$50.44m</strong> in total.</li>
<li><strong>$34.99m</strong> of that is now guaranteed, the first three seasons.</li>
<li>Philadelphia exercised the 2027-28 option in October 2026, and the final year is still a club option.</li>
<li>He earns more in one season than most second-round picks earn in four.</li>
</ul>
<p>At 21 he is the second youngest player Philadelphia is paying.</p>

